check.output:
✅ Active suite switched to: {activate_argument}
Status: {suite_status}
Stories: (list story files from the suite entry)

All subsequent commands will use this suite unless you pass a suite name explicitly.

step.action:
Ensure TestResult/ folder exists (create if missing).
Read TestResult/test-suites.yml (if it exists).
CASE A — Suite "{suite_name}" does NOT yet exist in the file: Append a new entry: - name: {suite_name} status: story-analyzed created: {current_date} updated: {current_date} stories: (one line per story file in {story_files}) phases: analyze-story: done generate-test-cases: pending generate-e2e: pending generate-test-data: pending run-tests: pending analyze-bugs: pending generate-report: pending Set active_suite: {suite_name}
CASE B — Suite "{suite_name}" ALREADY EXISTS in the file: Update the existing entry: - stories: replace with current {story_files} list - phases.analyze-story: done - updated: {current_date} - status: keep existing status unchanged (do not downgrade) Set active_suite: {suite_name}
Write the updated content back to TestResult/test-suites.yml.

step.output:
📋 Suite registry updated: TestResult/test-suites.yml

Suite  : {suite_name}
Status : {suite_status}
Stories: (list story files)
Active : ✅ yes

Next step → /aiqa-generatetestcases to generate test cases (Phase 2)
